# PNB RuPay Select Imperial Debit Card: A Complete Guide

Sharing a complete guide on how to get the PNB RuPay Select Imperial Debit Card, order additional cards, and make the most of the vouchers.

## 1. Opening the Account

First, open a **PNB Elite Executive account**. You can open it either online or offline.

- No initial funding is required.
- You don't necessarily have to maintain the MAB (Monthly Average Balance).
- If you don't maintain the required MAB, your account may be downgraded, and AMC (Annual Maintenance Charges) will apply to the primary card.
- If you maintain the required MAB, the primary card has **zero AMC**.
- If you open any other type of account, you may not be eligible to get the Imperial Debit Card, either as your primary card or as an add-on card.

**Important:** Make sure you specifically open an Elite Executive account.

## 2. Getting the Card and Ordering Additional Cards

After opening the account, it may take around **20 days** to receive your first Imperial Debit Card.

Once you receive the first card, you can order two additional cards.

Here's how to do it:

1. Open the Elite Executive account and wait for your first card to arrive.
2. After receiving the first card, order the second card.
3. Once the second card arrives, order the third card.

Each additional card costs **₹708 as an issuance fee**.

### AMC details

- **Primary card:** No AMC if you maintain the required MAB. Otherwise, AMC is ₹900 + GST.
- **Additional cards:** AMC applies regardless of whether you maintain the required MAB.

Following this process, you can get three Imperial Debit Cards in total.

## 3. Registering the Cards on RuPay Truztee

After receiving your cards, register them on the RuPay Truztee website to access the available vouchers and benefits.

**You'll need three separate Truztee accounts for your three cards.**

Each account must have a different:
- Mobile number
- Email ID

The reason is that all three cards share the same first six digits (BIN). If you try to add another card to the same account, the website may show an error saying that the card has already been added.

Therefore, use a separate mobile number and email address for each card's registration.

## 4. Vouchers and Benefits

One of the main attractions of this card is the vouchers.

**You get the available vouchers on all three cards**, so registering all three cards allows you to access the benefits associated with each card.

The available vouchers include brands such as:
- Reliance
- BigBasket
- Kalyan
- Decathlon
- Myntra
- Amazon/OTT benefits, is the 1499 membership.

### Voucher validity

An important detail: vouchers for brands such as Reliance, BigBasket, Kalyan, Decathlon, and Myntra reportedly have a validity of **one year**, rather than the one-month validity mentioned in some places.

For BigBasket, Myntra, and Decathlon, you can add the vouchers to the respective wallets, where applicable, and use them later.

For more information and community discussion about voucher validity, refer to this guide:

https://www.reddit.com/r/CreditCardsIndia/comments/1u8k7nd/guide-pnb-imperial-elite-executive-debit-card/

## 5. Final Tips

Before getting started, keep these points in mind:

- Open an **Elite Executive account**, not a regular account.
- Wait for your first card before ordering the second one.
- Order the third card only after receiving the second.
- Keep three separate mobile numbers and email IDs ready for Truztee registration.
- Remember that additional cards have AMC even if you maintain the required MAB.
- Check the voucher terms and expiry dates when redeeming them.

That's pretty much the process! If you're planning to get the PNB RuPay Select Imperial Debit Card, these are the main things to know to get all three cards and make the most of their voucher benefits.

